  <title>Invoice</title>

  <p>Open a new invoice with <guiseq><gui>Customer</gui><gui>New
  invoice</gui></guiseq>, the <gui>New Invoice</gui> button of the main
  window, or <keyseq><key>Ctrl</key><key>I</key></keyseq>. Everything typed on
  an invoice is saved as you go, so you can close the window and finish the
  invoice later: it waits under <link xref="draft_invoices">Draft
  invoices</link> until it is posted.</p>

  <section id="customer">
  <title>Choosing the customer</title>
  <p>Pick the customer from the list, or type part of the name. The address,
  phone, email and <gui>Unpaid</gui> balance are filled in. If the customer
  already has an invoice that was never posted, it is opened instead of a new
  one. If there are several, the <link xref="#document_list">document
  list</link> opens so you can choose.</p>
  <list>
    <item><p><gui>Customer</gui> opens the contacts window. Right click in the
    customer box and choose <gui>Contact hub</gui> to see everything about
    this customer.</p></item>
    <item><p><gui>Email</gui> opens <link xref="send_email"/> with a new
    message to the customer.</p></item>
    <item><p>The shipping box chooses which of the customer's shipping
    addresses goes on the invoice.</p></item>
    <item><p><gui>Location :</gui> is where the stock is taken from when the
    invoice is posted.</p></item>
  </list>
  </section>

  <section id="lines">
  <title>Adding products</title>
  <steps>
    <item><p>Click <gui>New Item</gui>, or press <key>F2</key>.</p></item>
    <item><p>Type the quantity and press <key>Tab</key> to move to the
    product.</p></item>
    <item><p>Pick the product from the list, or type part of its name. Only
    products marked as sellable are listed. The price is the customer's price
    for that product.</p></item>
    <item><p>Press <key>Tab</key> to move on to <gui>Remark</gui> and
    <gui>Price</gui> if they need changing.</p></item>
  </steps>
  <p>Products counted in inventory, and products with serial numbers, can only
  be sold in whole units. A fraction is refused with a message.</p>
  <p>Right click a line for more:</p>
  <terms>
    <item><title><gui>Delete item</gui> (<key>F3</key>)</title>
    <p>Removes the line.</p></item>
    <item><title><gui>Move up</gui>, <gui>Move down</gui>
    (<keyseq><key>Ctrl</key><key>Up</key></keyseq>,
    <keyseq><key>Ctrl</key><key>Down</key></keyseq>)</title>
    <p>Change the order the lines print in.</p></item>
    <item><title><gui>Product hub</gui>
    (<keyseq><key>Ctrl</key><key>H</key></keyseq>)</title>
    <p>Opens the <link xref="product_hub">product hub</link> for the line's
    product.</p></item>
    <item><title><gui>Refresh price</gui></title>
    <p>Puts the customer's current price back on the line, undoing a typed
    price.</p></item>
    <item><title><gui>Cancel time clock import</gui></title>
    <p>Only shown on a line imported from the time clock. The hours become
    available to import again; the line itself stays until you delete
    it.</p></item>
  </terms>
  </section>

  <section id="barcode">
  <title>Scanning barcodes</title>
  <p>Scan into the <gui>Scan barcode</gui> box below the lines. Each scan adds
  one of the product, on its existing line if it already has one. Barcodes
  that match no product are collected in the <gui>Barcode error!</gui>
  window, with how many times each was scanned.</p>
  <list>
    <item><p><keyseq><key>Shift</key><key>Enter</key></keyseq> after a scan
    takes one off that product's line instead.</p></item>
    <item><p><keyseq><key>Ctrl</key><key>Enter</key></keyseq> after a scan
    changes the selected line to that product.</p></item>
  </list>
  </section>

  <section id="serial_numbers">
  <title>Serial numbers</title>
  <p>When a product needs serial numbers on its invoice, the serial number
  box opens beside the lines. Select the line, type or scan each serial number
  into <gui>Serial number</gui> and press <key>Enter</key>. Until each line
  has as many serial numbers as its quantity, the post button reads
  <gui>Qty/serial number mismatch</gui> and cannot be clicked.</p>
  <p>A serial number is refused if it is already on another invoice, or if it
  was never made or received. To add one by hand, use
  <guiseq><gui>General</gui><gui>Serial numbers</gui></guiseq>. <gui>Remove
  serial number</gui> takes the selected one off the line.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="tax">
  <title>Tax exemptions</title>
  <p>Choose the customer's exemption from the box beside <gui>Tax
  exemption</gui>, and every line is taxed with it. The <gui>Tax
  exemption</gui> button opens <link xref="tax_exemptions"/> to give the
  customer another one.</p>
  <p>The box starts on the customer's newest exemption. Products posted from a
  <link xref="job_sheet">job sheet</link> take that exemption too. A product
  with <gui>Tax exemptible</gui> unchecked is taxed at its own rate whatever is
  chosen.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="post">
  <title>Posting</title>
  <steps>
    <item><p>Check the <gui>Invoice Date</gui>. Click the icon in it to choose
    another date from the calendar.</p></item>
    <item><p>Click <gui>Post Invoice</gui>. The print dialog opens.</p></item>
    <item><p>Print, and the invoice is posted: the stock leaves the chosen
    location, the sale goes into the books and the window closes.</p></item>
  </steps>
  <p>To change your mind, check <gui>Cancel printing and posting</gui> on the
  <gui>PyGtk Posting</gui> tab of the print dialog, then click
  <gui>Print</gui>. Nothing is printed or posted. Closing the print dialog
  with <gui>Cancel</gui> instead still posts the invoice, without printing
  it.</p>
  <p>Posting is refused if the invoice has no lines or no location is chosen.
  If the sale takes a product's stock below zero, you are asked whether to
  post anyway.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="menu">
  <title>The invoice menu</title>
  <terms>
    <item><title><gui>Cancel</gui></title>
    <p>Closes the window. The invoice is kept as a draft.</p></item>
    <item><title><gui>Document list</gui></title>
    <p>Opens the <link xref="#document_list">document list</link>.</p></item>
    <item><title><gui>Email invoice</gui></title>
    <p>When checked, posting opens <link xref="send_email"/> addressed to
    the customer, with the invoice attached and the message set in <link
    xref="email_message"/>. It is greyed out for a customer with no email
    address. The setting in <guiseq><gui>Edit</gui><gui>Settings</gui></guiseq>
    decides whether it starts checked.</p></item>
    <item><title><gui>Fax invoice...</gui></title>
    <p>Confirms a fax number before posting; the invoice is faxed as soon as
    it is posted. See <link xref="fax#invoice"/>.</p></item>
    <item><title><gui>Import time clock</gui></title>
    <p>See <link xref="#time_clock"/>.</p></item>
    <item><title><gui>Packing list</gui></title>
    <p>Shows a pick sheet of the lines, without prices. It does not post or
    print the invoice.</p></item>
    <item><title><gui>Print without confirming</gui></title>
    <p>When checked, posting prints straight to the printer with no print
    dialog, so there is no chance to cancel. The setting in
    <guiseq><gui>Edit</gui><gui>Settings</gui></guiseq> decides whether it
    starts checked.</p></item>
    <item><title><gui>Products</gui></title>
    <p>Opens the <link xref="products">products</link> window.</p></item>
    <item><title><gui>Refresh all prices</gui></title>
    <p>Puts the customer's current price back on every line.</p></item>
    <item><title><gui>Transfer invoice</gui></title>
    <p>Moves this invoice to another customer. The shipping address is
    cleared, because it belonged to the first customer.</p></item>
    <item><title><gui>View invoice</gui></title>
    <p>Shows the invoice as it would print, without posting it.</p></item>
  </terms>
  </section>

  <section id="document_list">
  <title>The document list</title>
  <p>A customer can have several unposted invoices at once, for instance a
  quote and an invoice. The <gui>Document list</gui> window beside the
  invoice lists them. Double click one to work on it.</p>
  <list>
    <item><p>Click the <gui>Type</gui> to rename the kind of document, for
    instance to Quote. The first three letters start the document's
    name.</p></item>
    <item><p>Uncheck <gui>Active</gui> to keep a document but leave it off
    the main window's draft count.</p></item>
    <item><p><gui>New Invoice</gui> starts another invoice for the same
    customer.</p></item>
    <item><p><gui>Delete Invoice</gui> deletes the selected document after
    asking. A posted invoice cannot be deleted here.</p></item>
  </list>
  </section>

  <section id="time_clock">
  <title>Importing time clock hours</title>
  <p><gui>Import time clock</gui> lists the hours punched on this customer's
  job sheets that have not been invoiced.</p>
  <steps>
    <item><p>Check <gui>Import</gui> on the entries to bill. <gui>Select
    all</gui> and <gui>Unselect all</gui> check or clear them all. The total
    is rounded up to the next tenth of an hour.</p></item>
    <item><p>Choose the product to bill the hours as in <gui>Import as</gui>,
    and change the <gui>Description</gui> if needed.</p></item>
    <item><p>Click <gui>Post to Invoice</gui>. One line is added for the
    rounded hours, at the customer's price for that product.</p></item>
  </steps>
  </section>

  <section id="posted">
  <title>Changing a posted invoice</title>
  <p>A posted invoice opened again, for instance from <link
  xref="unpaid_invoices"/>, can still be changed. Each change is saved at once
  and followed into the stock and the books. If the change takes stock below
  zero you are told, but the change is already saved.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="others">
  <title>Changes made on another computer</title>
  <p>If someone else changes the invoice you have open, a bar says
  <gui>There are changes on this Invoice</gui>. Click <gui>Reload</gui> to see
  them. If the invoice is deleted or posted on the other computer, you are
  told and the window closes.</p>
  </section>

</page>
